description:
End Goal: Review Erwin’s proposed approach for measuring editor delays, setting due dates, introducing a trial tracking period, and establishing a future penalty/bonus structure before discussing it with Malik.

Owner: Erwin to configure / Jane to coordinate
Approval: Malik before implementation
Due: Prepare this week; activate only after approval
Reference: 

The proposed framework is: Assignment → final video ready = measured editor turnaround

Then:
 automatically add a 3-working-day due date; 
 notify editors before measurement begins; 
 apply nothing retrospectively; 
 track results for two weeks; 
 no deductions during the pilot; 
 review the data afterward; 
 Malik + Manjeet determine any eventual penalty/bonus structure. 

The existing analysis found that some late orders had actually already been completed by the editor, so measuring the entire order journey would incorrectly assign responsibility.

Done when: The tracking logic and rollout instructions are ready, but nothing financial is implemented without Malik/Manjeet approval.
